When calling `vscode.window.showQuickPick` with custom type items, `onDidSelectItem` callback cannot be correctly typed:
```typescript
interface MyPickItem extends vscode.QuickPickItem { }
var items:MyPickItem[];
vscode.window.showQuickPick(items, { 
    placeHolder: "(placeholder)", 
    onDidSelectItem: (item:MyPickItem) => {
        /* Wont copile, error:
            Argument of type '{ placeHolder: string; onDidSelectItem: (item: MyPickItem) => void; }' is not assignable to parameter of type 'QuickPickOptions'.
            Types of property 'onDidSelectItem' are incompatible.
                Type '(item: MyPickItem) => void' is not assignable to type '<T extends QuickPickItem>(item: string | T) => any'.
                Types of parameters 'item' and 'item' are incompatible.
                    Type 'string | T' is not assignable to type 'MyPickItem'.
                    Type 'string' is not assignable to type 'MyPickItem'.
        */
    }
});
```
That because of way which typescript handles generic constraints ( https://github.com/Microsoft/TypeScript/issues/3410#issuecomment-111646030 ). So easy fix to make it usable is to just change constraint to base QuickPickItem interface.

PR for #31358

API to read and write configuration value given a resource 

## How to use

```ts
let configuration = vscode.workspace.getConfiguration('testExtension');

// Read
// Effective value (Default / Gloabl / Workspace)
let value = configuration.get('resourceConfiguration')

// Inspecting
// folderValue is always undefined
let { defaultValue, globalValue, workspaceValue, folderValue } = configuration.inspect('resourceConfiguration');

// Writing to Global configuration
// Error when the configuration is invalid
configuration.update('resourceConfiguration', false, ConfigurationTarget.Global);
configuration.update('resourceConfiguration', false, true);

// Writing to Workspace configuration
// Error when 
// the configuration is invalid
// there is no workspace (Invalid target)
configuration.update('resourceConfiguration', true, ConfigurationTarget.Workspace);
configuration.update('resourceConfiguration', true);
configuration.update('resourceConfiguration', true, false);

// Writing to Workspace Folder configuration - Always returns error since there is no resource
configuration.update('resourceConfiguration', false, ConfigurationTarget.WorkspaceFolder);

// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ //

// Reading and Writing a configuration given a resource
let configuration = vscode.workspace.getConfiguration('testExtension', vscode.window.activeTextEditor.document.uri);

// Read
// Effective value (Default / Gloabl / Workspace / Folder)
let value = configuration.get('resourceConfiguration')

// Inspecting
// folderValue is undefined when
// the resource does not belong to any workspace folder
// the workspace folder containing the resource has not defined any value of the configuration
let { defaultValue, globalValue, workspaceValue, folderValue } = configuration.inspect('resourceConfiguration');

// Writing to Global configuration
// Error when the configuration is invalid
configuration.update('resourceConfiguration', false, ConfigurationTarget.Global);
configuration.update('resourceConfiguration', false, true);

// Writing to Workspace configuration
// the configuration is invalid
// there is no workspace (Invalid target)
configuration.update('resourceConfiguration', true, ConfigurationTarget.Workspace);
configuration.update('resourceConfiguration', true);
configuration.update('resourceConfiguration', true, false);

// Writing to Workspace folder configuration
// Error when
// the configuration is invalid
// there is no workspace (Invalid target)
// the configuration is workbench configuration (Invalid configuration)
// the resource does not belong to any workspace folder (Invalid target)
configuration.update('resourceConfiguration', false, ConfigurationTarget.WorkspaceFolder);
```
